//? Title: Gabow SCC: open vertices, candidate boundaries and active DFS
//? Subtitle: Actual two-stack events, sink-first component labels and an amortized linear traversal
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
A directed graph's strongly connected components are its maximal mutually
reachable vertex sets. Gabow's path-based algorithm finds them with one DFS,
an open-vertex stack and a stack of candidate component boundaries.
A three-vertex example exposes the distinction between open vertices and active
DFS calls. Native snapshots then preserve the original eight-vertex example,
including its raw component IDs, and construct its quotient graph.
Controlled neighbor-order, loop and duplicate-edge changes separate partition
meaning from labels and traversal work. Independent reachability checks,
actual operation counts and conservative owned-history admission make the
correctness and resource claims explicit.
)

\toc

> A finished DFS call can still be open

Use adjacency rows 0→[1,2], 1→[0], 2→[1], in that order.
DFS enters 0, then 1. The edge 1→0 collapses candidate 1 into candidate 0.
The call for 1 finishes, but 1 remains unassigned on the open stack S.
Later the edge 2→1 reaches that finished-yet-open vertex and merges 2 into the
same unfinished component. All three vertices are mutually reachable.

The active DFS frames, S and boundary stack B are different objects.
S contains every discovered vertex not yet assigned a component; it can retain
vertices whose calls have returned. B contains the surviving candidate roots.
The following diagram reads actual snapshots from one execution, without replay.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/gabow_tiny.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/gabow_scc.hpp>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/graph_connectivity.hpp>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/depth_first_search.hpp>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/brute_force_search.hpp>
#include <datamunge/plot/diagram.hpp>
#include <algorithm>
#include <array>
#include <cmath>
#include <limits>
#include <print>
namespace dm=datamunge;
int main(){
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
  const dm::algorithms::SccAdjacency graph{{1,2},{0},{1}};
  const auto t=dm::algorithms::gabow_scc_trace(3,graph,263);
  std::print("| event | kind | u | target or assigned v | open S | boundaries B | active (vertex,next) |\n| ---: | --- | ---: | ---: | --- | --- | --- |\n");
  for(std::size_t i=0;i<t.events.size();++i){const auto& e=t.events[i];std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} |\n",i,e.kind,e.u,e.v,e.path,e.roots,e.stack);}
  std::print("\nRaw labels {}; components {}; actual transitions {}; peak DFS {}; peak open S {}; peak B {}; actual retained entries {}.\n",t.components,t.work.component_closures,t.work.event_count,t.work.peak_dfs,t.work.peak_open,t.work.peak_roots,t.captured_entries);
  const auto finished=std::find_if(t.events.begin(),t.events.end(),[](const auto& e){return e.kind=="finish"&&e.u==1;});
  const auto cross=std::find_if(t.events.begin(),t.events.end(),[](const auto& e){return e.kind=="edge"&&e.u==2&&e.v==1;});
  const auto merged=std::find_if(t.events.begin(),t.events.end(),[](const auto& e){return e.kind=="collapse"&&e.u==2&&e.v==1;});
  if(finished==t.events.end()||cross==t.events.end()||merged==t.events.end())throw std::runtime_error("missing actual transition");
  dm::graphics::Diagram d(61,1100);dm::graphics::DiagramNodeStyle box;box.width=4.5;box.height=2.5;box.font_size=21;
  d.node("finished",{0,0},std::format("DFS 1 finished\nS = {}\nB = {}\nframes = {}",finished->path,finished->roots,finished->stack),box)
   .node("edge",{6.1,0},std::format("Examine 2 -> 1\nS = {}\nB = {}\nframes = {}",cross->path,cross->roots,cross->stack),box)
   .node("merge",{12.2,0},std::format("Pop boundary 2\nS = {}\nB = {}\nframes = {}",merged->path,merged->roots,merged->stack),box)
   .edge("finished","edge","enter 2").edge("edge","merge","open target")
   .text({6.1,3},"Actual open vertices and active calls are different",27)
   .text({6.1,-2.6},std::format("Vertex 1 stays open after its DFS returns; final labels {}",t.components),25)
   .save_svg("build/gabow_tiny.svg");
  if(t.components!=std::vector<int>{0,0,0}||t.work.peak_open!=3||t.work.peak_dfs!=2)throw std::runtime_error("finished-open control");
}
```
