Original labels [3, 3, 2, 2, 2, 1, 1, 0]; components 4; Kosaraju agrees true; raw internal edges 7; raw cross edges 3; unique quotient arcs 3; reverse topological true.

| raw component ID | original vertices | size | quotient neighbor indices |
| ---: | --- | ---: | --- |
| 0 | [7] | 1 | [] |
| 1 | [5, 6] | 2 | [0] |
| 2 | [2, 3, 4] | 3 | [1] |
| 3 | [0, 1] | 2 | [2] |

Actual work: 8 visits; 10 examined edges; tree 7; open 3; closed 0; boundary collapses 4; closures 4; events 42; retained entries 1173.
\image(figures/gabow_original.svg)
// result_end
\caption(The original graph contracts to a four-node chain with component sizes 2,3,2,1 from source to sink. Sink-first IDs decrease left to right; quotient arcs omit internal edges and deduplicate cross entries.)
\alttext(A native directed chain shows raw component3 containing0 and1, component2 containing2,3,4, component1 containing5 and6, and component0 containing7.)

The links1→2,4→5,6→7 are tree edges in this traversal. Their downstream
components close before the parent calls return; they do not create an open
return path that would merge the groups. The original output's component labels
are preserved exactly, while partition comparison correctly ignores label names.

> Labels, duplicate entries and what the quotient can certify

Reversing the neighbor order of0→[1,2] changes the closure order of the two
unrelated sinks, and hence their raw IDs. The equivalence relation stays the same.
Self-loops and duplicate entries also preserve the partition, but each original
entry is still examined. An open-edge event means discovered and unassigned;
it need not be an edge to an active ancestor.

The summary validates shapes, endpoints and nonnegative labels. Its quotient
can still be cyclic when arbitrary supplied labels split a real SCC. It is a
presentation tool, not a second SCC algorithm or an independent correctness oracle.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/gabow_labels.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/gabow_scc.hpp>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/graph_connectivity.hpp>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/depth_first_search.hpp>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/brute_force_search.hpp>
#include <datamunge/plot/diagram.hpp>
#include <algorithm>
#include <array>
#include <cmath>
#include <limits>
#include <print>
namespace dm=datamunge;
int main(){
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
  const dm::algorithms::SccAdjacency a{{1,2},{},{}},b{{2,1},{},{}};
  const auto ca=dm::algorithms::gabow_scc(3,a),cb=dm::algorithms::gabow_scc(3,b);
  std::print("Neighbor order: first labels {}; reversed labels {}; same partition {}; identical label vectors {}.\n",ca,cb,dm::algorithms::scc_same_partition(ca,cb),ca==cb);
  const dm::algorithms::SccAdjacency simple{{1},{0,2},{}},repeated{{1,1,0},{0,0,1,2,2},{2}};
  const auto one=dm::algorithms::gabow_scc_work(3,simple);
  const auto many=dm::algorithms::gabow_scc_work(3,repeated);
  const auto q=dm::algorithms::scc_summary(repeated,many.components);
  std::print("Loops and duplicates: base labels {}; changed labels {}; same partition {}; raw internal {}; raw cross {}; unique quotient arcs {}.\n",one.components,many.components,dm::algorithms::scc_same_partition(one.components,many.components),q.internal_edges,q.cross_edges,q.unique_cross_edges);
  std::print("\n| input | tree edges | open edges | closed edges | examined entries |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n");
  std::print("| Base | {} | {} | {} | {} |\n",one.work.tree_edges,one.work.open_edges,one.work.closed_edges,one.work.edges_examined);
  std::print("| Loops and duplicates | {} | {} | {} | {} |\n",many.work.tree_edges,many.work.open_edges,many.work.closed_edges,many.work.edges_examined);
  const auto arbitrary=dm::algorithms::scc_summary({{1},{0}},{0,1});
  std::print("\nArbitrary split of a two-vertex cycle: quotient {}; reverse topological {}. The summary does not certify supplied SCC labels.\n",arbitrary.adjacency,arbitrary.reverse_topological);
  auto base=dm::graphics::RPlot::barplot({double(one.work.tree_edges),double(one.work.open_edges),double(one.work.closed_edges)},{"Tree","Open","Closed"});
  base.title("Base: three examined entries").xlab("Actual edge-decision category").ylab("Entries").y_limits(0,7);
  auto changed=dm::graphics::RPlot::barplot({double(many.work.tree_edges),double(many.work.open_edges),double(many.work.closed_edges)},{"Tree","Open","Closed"});
  changed.title("Same partition: nine examined entries").xlab("Actual edge-decision category").ylab("Entries").y_limits(0,7);
  dm::graphics::RLayout::create(1,2).add(base).add(changed).size(1100,520).title("Loops and duplicates change executed work").fit_panels().save_svg("build/gabow_labels.svg");
  if(ca==cb||!dm::algorithms::scc_same_partition(ca,cb)||!dm::algorithms::scc_same_partition(one.components,many.components))throw std::runtime_error("label-independent meaning");
}
